  <hasMajorDescription rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">The Korean Studies major provides students with high-quality learning opportunities and an outstanding student experience in learning Korean. With the rapid economic development of the Republic of Korea (South Korea), and its position as the third biggest trading partner for Western Australia, Korean Studies is an increasingly important area of study. Korean Studies equips students with solid language skills and a broad in-depth knowledge of Korea, its society and people. Students will graduate with an in-depth understanding of the increasingly globalising world, as well as a versatile portfolio of skills and aptitudes which enhance employability.

This intermediate stream is designed for students who have completed ATAR Korean or equivalent. Students should be aware that this major does not provide a pathway to an Honours.</hasMajorDescription>
