  <hasCoreUnits rdf:resource="#AGRI1001"/>
  <hasCoreUnits rdf:resource="#SCIE1104"/>
  <hasCoreUnits rdf:resource="#SCOM1101"/>
  <hasCoreUnits rdf:resource="#AGRI2201"/>
  <hasCoreUnits rdf:resource="#GEOG2201"/>
  <hasCoreUnits rdf:resource="#SCIE2205"/>
  <hasCoreUnits rdf:resource="#AGRI3003"/>
  <hasCoreUnits rdf:resource="#ECON3300"/>
  <hasCoreUnits rdf:resource="#GEOG3301"/>
  <hasCoreUnits rdf:resource="#SCIE3314"/>
  <hasMajorCode rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">MJD-AGTEC</hasMajorCode>
  <hasMajorTitle rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Agricultural Technology</hasMajorTitle>
  <hasMajorSchool rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Agriculture and Environment</hasMajorSchool>
  <hasMajorDescription rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">There is a critical need to produce food and fibre more efficiently and sustainably. There are now rapid changes in the agricultural sector, largely due to developments in agricultural technologies in automation and remote sensing. This data-intensive technology has the potential to significantly increase production efficiency and reduce the environmental impact from agriculture; however, the key is making sense of the data and developing profitable and sustainable farming strategies. The Agricultural Technology major provides a broad agricultural background along with the necessary skills in data management and analysis, geographic information systems (GIS) and remote sensing. In this major, you will develop skills to integrate data analysis and knowledge of complex agricultural systems to make decisions for improved efficiency and profitability.</hasMajorDescription>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

