  <hasMajorCode rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">MJD-CMPSC</hasMajorCode>
  <hasMajorTitle rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Computer Science</hasMajorTitle>
  <hasMajorSchool rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Physics, Mathematics and Computing</hasMajorSchool>
  <hasMajorDescription rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Computing software and systems are becoming increasingly integral to our lives, revolutionising the world in which we live, work and communicate. This major provides its students with the knowledge and skills required to participate in this revolution. Your studies develop your knowledge of theoretical, algorithmic, implementation and systems principles that underpin computer languages and networks. If you wish to play a role in developing new computing technologies or specialise in enterprise-level programming, systems, software engineering or research careers, then Computer Science is the major for you.
The Computer Science major (MJD-CMPSC) in any course leading to a Bachelor of Science or Bachelor of Philosophy is accredited by the Australian Computer Society (ACS) for quality, career enablement and compliance with the Australian Computing Society (ACS) and international Seoul Accord graduate standards.</hasMajorDescription>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

