  <hasUnitCode rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">CHEM3101</hasUnitCode>
  <hasUnitTitle rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Workplace Safety and Advanced Analytical Methods</hasUnitTitle>
  <hasUnitSchool rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Molecular Sciences</hasUnitSchool>
  <hasUnitLevel rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3</hasUnitLevel>
  <hasUnitDescription rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">This unit builds upon CHEM2101-Analytical Methods and introduces students to topics relevant to the chemical industry, including advanced analytical methods and characterisation techniques. In addition, students are introduced to important aspects of occupational health and safety that are relevant to industry and the chemical laboratory, including legislation. This unit also further develops key scientific writing techniques with an emphasis on safety.
This unit will be offered from Semester 1 2025</hasUnitDescription>
