  <hasUnitOutcomes rdf:resource="#demonstrate an understanding of the basic physical operation of networks, including the concepts of data encoding and error detection and recovery."/>
  <hasUnitOutcomes rdf:resource="#explain the design motivation for, and operation of, contemporary wide-area, local-area and wireless networking technologies."/>
  <hasUnitOutcomes rdf:resource="#understand the TCP/IP protocol stack, and its support for client/server and peer-to-peer networking models."/>
  <hasUnitOutcomes rdf:resource="#apply industry standard networking programming interfaces from within procedural and object-oriented programming languages."/>
  <hasUnitOutcomes rdf:resource="#develop distributed applications for heterogeneous computer systems."/>
  <hasUnitOutcomes rdf:resource="#understand the security and privacy factors raised by contemporary networks and their applications."/>
  <hasUnitAssessments rdf:resource="#mid-semester test"/>
