  <hasUnitOutcomes rdf:resource="#know the physical basis of the climate system and mechanisms of anthropogenic climate change and variability."/>
  <hasUnitOutcomes rdf:resource="#interpret land surface data from measurement of key Australian ecosystems."/>
  <hasUnitOutcomes rdf:resource="#understand the changes in climate over the past, present and future."/>
  <hasUnitOutcomes rdf:resource="#communicate climate change and appreciate skepticism."/>
  <hasUnitOutcomes rdf:resource="#synthesise the physical understanding of the climate system and feedbacks witihin."/>
  <hasUnitAssessments rdf:resource="#practical exercise or practical report for each of 5 practical's total to take place approximately one every two weeks, with one in the first two weeks"/>
  <hasUnitAssessments rdf:resource="#a research report based on interpreting land surface data from a key Australian ecosystem"/>
  <hasContactRequirement rdf:resource="#contactrequirement710"/>
  <hasContactRequirement rdf:resource="#contactrequirement711"/>
  <hasUnitCode rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">ENVT2220</hasUnitCode>
  <hasUnitTitle rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">The Climate System</hasUnitTitle>
  <hasUnitSchool rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Agriculture and Environment</hasUnitSchool>
  <hasUnitLevel rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</hasUnitLevel>
  <hasUnitDescription rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">This unit investigates the physical basis of the climate system and mechanisms of anthropogenic climate change and variability. Importance is placed on the role of the land surface in the climate system including the carbon cycle, land use change and urbanisation.  Processes such as the greenhouse effect, aerosols, the El Nino-Southern Oscillation, climate feedbacks and rapid climate change are examined. Paleo, historical and climate model data are presented and assessed. Likely future climate changes are addressed and option for adaptation and mitigation for human society.</hasUnitDescription>
  <hasCreditPoints rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">6</hasCreditPoints>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

