  <hasUnitLevel rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3</hasUnitLevel>
  <hasUnitDescription rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">This unit is an introduction to the modelling and properties of biological, physical and engineering systems that change with time and which are mathematically described by difference equations and differential equations. Concepts discussed include stability, bifurcations and chaos, stable manifolds, periodic orbits, crisis and universality.</hasUnitDescription>
