  <hasUnitOutcomes rdf:resource="#describe and recognise structural components of the body in gross anatomical terms."/>
  <hasUnitOutcomes rdf:resource="#describe the overall body plan and the organisational levels in the structure of the human body, from cells to organ systems."/>
  <hasUnitOutcomes rdf:resource="#outline the basic structure and function of primary tissues - epithelium, connective tissue, muscle and nervous tissue - at the gross and microscopic level."/>
  <hasUnitOutcomes rdf:resource="#describe the gross and microscopic structure of the integumentary, musculoskeletal, nervous, cardiovascular, circulatory, respiratory, and reproductive/genital systems."/>
  <hasUnitOutcomes rdf:resource="#describe the functions of the integumentary, musculoskeletal, nervous, cardiovascular, circulatory, respiratory, and reproductive/genital systems."/>
  <hasUnitOutcomes rdf:resource="#describe physiological control systems, including the endocrine system and the autonomic nervous system."/>
  <hasUnitOutcomes rdf:resource="#describe key processes in cell biology, including cell membrane function and transport processes, nerve impulse generation, transmission and processing, and muscle excitation and contraction."/>
